{
  "changelog": "**Major update: Expanded documentation, stricter usage rules, and improved invocation protocol for Informat platform operations.**\n\n- Overhauled in-skill documentation directory: added comprehensive, official feature and script API docs under `references/doc/markdown/`.\n- Increased method support from 119 to 215, reflecting broader platform capabilities.\n- Replaced all legacy developer hints, usage of sample `.env`, and fixed relative paths with an absolute-path invocation protocol tied to the current session\u2019s runtime instruction.\n- Introduced a unified \u201cgate\u201d protocol: first write in each domain requires reading design doc + schema with explicit proof (`_doc_ack`, `_ack`). Subsequent writes in that domain are ungated but still validate parameters locally.\n- Clarified handling for specialized gates (script SDK docs, platform expressions, blueprint checks) and error outputs; provided clear instructions for each.\n- Updated method interface prefix rules for agent selection; clarified parameter passing (`--threadId`, `--appId`).\n- Deprecated references to old knowledge files, environment setup, and vague placeholders; standardized all references and invocations for reliability",
